After installing the newer pgvector build, run this in each database that has the extension:

```sql
ALTER EXTENSION vector UPDATE;
```

This upgrades the extension to the newest version the installed files support. To target a specific version, use `ALTER EXTENSION vector UPDATE TO '<version>';`.

To check the result, compare the installed and available versions:

```sql
SELECT extversion FROM pg_extension WHERE extname = 'vector';
SELECT version FROM pg_available_extensions WHERE name = 'vector';
```
